#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:1
msgid "Release 0.10 (2006-10-06)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:3
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:5
msgid ""
"This version of Nix uses Berkeley DB 4.4 instead of 4.3. The database is "
"upgraded automatically, but you should be careful not to use old versions of "
"Nix that still use Berkeley DB 4.3. In particular, if you use a Nix "
"installed through Nix, you should run"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:12
msgid "first."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:14
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:16
msgid ""
"Also, the database schema has changed slighted to fix a performance issue "
"(see below). When you run any Nix 0.10 command for the first time, the "
"database will be upgraded automatically. This is irreversible."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:21
msgid "`nix-env` usability improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:23
msgid ""
"An option `--compare-versions` (or `-c`) has been added to `nix-"
"env                                                 --query` to allow you to "
"compare installed versions of packages to available versions, or vice versa. "
"An easy way to see if you are up to date with what’s in your subscribed "
"channels is `nix-env -qc \\*`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:30
msgid ""
"`nix-env --query` now takes as arguments a list of package names about which "
"to show information, just like `--install`, etc.: for example, `nix-env -q "
"gcc`. Note that to show all derivations, you need to specify `\\*`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:35
msgid ""
"`nix-env -i                                                 pkgname` will "
"now install the highest available version of _pkgname_, rather than "
"installing all available versions (which would probably give collisions) "
"(`NIX-31`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:40
msgid ""
"`nix-env (-i|-u) --dry-run` now shows exactly which missing paths will be "
"built or substituted."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:43
msgid ""
"`nix-env -qa --description` shows human-readable descriptions of packages, "
"provided that they have a `meta.description` attribute (which most packages "
"in Nixpkgs don’t have yet)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:47
msgid "New language features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:49
msgid ""
"Reference scanning (which happens after each build) is much faster and takes "
"a constant amount of memory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:52
msgid "String interpolation. Expressions like"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:54
msgid ""
"    \"--with-freetype2-library=\" + freetype + \"/lib\"\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:56
msgid "can now be written as"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:58
msgid ""
"    \"--with-freetype2-library=${freetype}/lib\"\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:60
msgid ""
"You can write arbitrary expressions within `${...}`, not just identifiers."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:63
msgid "Multi-line string literals."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:65
msgid ""
"String concatenations can now involve derivations, as in the example `\"--"
"with-freetype2-library=\"                                                 + "
"freetype + \"/lib\"`. This was not previously possible because we need to "
"register that a derivation that uses such a string is dependent on "
"`freetype`. The evaluator now properly propagates this information. "
"Consequently, the subpath operator (`~`) has been deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:73
msgid ""
"Default values of function arguments can now refer to other function "
"arguments; that is, all arguments are in scope in the default values "
"(`NIX-45`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:77
msgid ""
"Lots of new built-in primitives, such as functions for list manipulation and "
"integer arithmetic. See the manual for a complete list. All primops are now "
"available in the set `builtins`, allowing one to test for the availability "
"of primop in a backwards-compatible way."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:83
msgid ""
"Real let-expressions: `let x "
"= ...;                                                 ... z = ...; in ...`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:86
msgid ""
"New commands `nix-pack-closure` and `nix-unpack-closure` than can be used to "
"easily transfer a store path with all its dependencies to another machine. "
"Very convenient whenever you have some package on your machine and you want "
"to copy it somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:91
msgid "XML support:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:93
msgid ""
"`nix-env -q --xml` prints the installed or available packages in an XML "
"representation for easy processing by other tools."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:96
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate --eval-only                                                 "
"--xml` prints an XML representation of the resulting term. (The new flag `--"
"strict` forces ‘deep’ evaluation of the result, i.e., list elements and "
"attributes are evaluated recursively.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:101
msgid ""
"In Nix expressions, the primop `builtins.toXML` converts a term to an XML "
"representation. This is primarily useful for passing structured information "
"to builders."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:105
msgid ""
"You can now unambiguously specify which derivation to build or install in "
"`nix-env`, `nix-instantiate` and `nix-build` using the `--attr` / `-A` "
"flags, which takes an attribute name as argument. (Unlike symbolic package "
"names such as `subversion-1.4.0`, attribute names in an attribute set are "
"unique.) For instance, a quick way to perform a test build of a package in "
"Nixpkgs is `nix-build         pkgs/top-level/all-packages.nix -A         "
"foo`. `nix-env -q         --attr` shows the attribute names corresponding to "
"each derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:115
msgid ""
"If the top-level Nix expression used by `nix-env`, `nix-instantiate` or `nix-"
"build` evaluates to a function whose arguments all have default values, the "
"function will be called automatically. Also, the new command-line switch `--"
"arg         name         value` can be used to specify function arguments on "
"the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:123
msgid ""
"`nix-install-package --url         URL` allows a package to be installed "
"directly from the given URL."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:126
msgid ""
"Nix now works behind an HTTP proxy server; just set the standard environment "
"variables `http_proxy`, `https_proxy`, `ftp_proxy` or `all_proxy` "
"appropriately. Functions such as `fetchurl` in Nixpkgs also respect these "
"variables."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:131
msgid ""
"`nix-build -o         symlink` allows the symlink to the build result to be "
"named something other than `result`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:135
msgid "Platform support:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:137
msgid ""
"Support for 64-bit platforms, provided a [suitably patched ATerm library]"
"(http://bugzilla.sen.cwi.nl:8080/show_bug.cgi?id=606) is used. Also, files "
"larger than 2 GiB are now supported."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:141
msgid ""
"Added support for Cygwin (Windows, `i686-cygwin`), Mac OS X on Intel (`i686-"
"darwin`) and Linux on PowerPC (`powerpc-linux`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:144
msgid ""
"Users of SMP and multicore machines will appreciate that the number of "
"builds to be performed in parallel can now be specified in the configuration "
"file in the `build-max-jobs` setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:149
msgid "Garbage collector improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:151
msgid ""
"Open files (such as running programs) are now used as roots of the garbage "
"collector. This prevents programs that have been uninstalled from being "
"garbage collected while they are still running. The script that detects "
"these additional runtime roots (`find-runtime-roots.pl`) is inherently "
"system-specific, but it should work on Linux and on all platforms that have "
"the `lsof` utility."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:159
msgid ""
"`nix-store --gc` (a.k.a. `nix-collect-garbage`) prints out the number of "
"bytes freed on standard output. `nix-"
"store                                                 --gc --print-dead` "
"shows how many bytes would be freed by an actual garbage collection."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:164
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage -d` removes all old generations of _all_ profiles "
"before calling the actual garbage collector (`nix-"
"store                                                 --gc`). This is an "
"easy way to get rid of all old packages in the Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:169
msgid ""
"`nix-store` now has an operation `--delete` to delete specific paths from "
"the Nix store. It won’t delete reachable (non-garbage) paths unless `--"
"ignore-liveness` is specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:173
msgid ""
"Berkeley DB 4.4’s process registry feature is used to recover from crashed "
"Nix processes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:176
msgid ""
"A performance issue has been fixed with the `referer` table, which stores "
"the inverse of the `references` table (i.e., it tells you what store paths "
"refer to a given path). Maintaining this table could take a quadratic amount "
"of time, as well as a quadratic amount of Berkeley DB log file space (in "
"particular when running the garbage collector) (`NIX-23`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:183
msgid ""
"Nix now catches the `TERM` and `HUP` signals in addition to the `INT` "
"signal. So you can now do a `killall         nix-store` without triggering a "
"database recovery."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:187
msgid "`bsdiff` updated to version 4.3."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:189
msgid ""
"Substantial performance improvements in expression evaluation and `nix-env -"
"qa`, all thanks to [Valgrind](http://valgrind.org/). Memory use has been "
"reduced by a factor 8 or so. Big speedup by memoisation of path hashing."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:194
msgid "Lots of bug fixes, notably:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:196
msgid ""
"Make sure that the garbage collector can run successfully when the disk is "
"full (`NIX-18`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:199
msgid ""
"`nix-env` now locks the profile to prevent races between concurrent `nix-"
"env` operations on the same profile (`NIX-7`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:202
msgid ""
"Removed misleading messages from `nix-env -i` (e.g., "
"``installing                                                 `foo'`` "
"followed by ``uninstalling                                                 "
"`foo'``) (`NIX-17`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:207
msgid ""
"Nix source distributions are a lot smaller now since we no longer include a "
"full copy of the Berkeley DB source distribution (but only the bits we need)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.10.md:211
msgid ""
"Header files are now installed so that external programs can use the Nix "
"libraries."
msgstr ""
